    "Scouting Notes": "It's been a while, but he's been very solid in AA this season\n Definitely old for the level at 26, but impacting the ball a lot more this year\n Probably nothing, but can't say for sure, as the bat to ball skills are a bit better as well\n Still not much of a defender outside of first, though he is really solid there\n Likely AAAA type at best but perhaps a late bloomer",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/20/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "When drafted, Brewers announced him as a catcher.\n After spending a little time there in Low A and High A, he's spent the majority of the time at both corner infield spots. More at 1B lately.\n His third base defense is not very good. He can hold up at first though.\n The bat is what will potentially carry him through the system. \n He got off to a very slow start at High A but finished really strong to earn his promotion to AA.\n Walk rate has gone down and strikeout rate up at each stop. \n Power shows flashes but hasn't been consistent at all.\n Will need to show something in AA to really stay a relevant prospect.",
